  partName: Cylinder Head Bolt (6)
  description: The Cylinder Head Bolt (6) is a small, intricately shaped component
    situated at the top-center-center of the engine, constructed from Material.001.
    Its primary function is to provide additional securing force to the cylinder
    head, supplementing the engine's ability to contain high pressures and temperatures.
    Notably, the bolt's material properties allow it to maintain its structural integrity
    even in extreme operating conditions, ensuring a reliable engine performance.
